!
! Rolling-window totals (understory_rules.h UR3), in Trebago, one reading
! per row in order: each row's total is the exact sum of its own amount and
! the width - 1 before it (fewer at the start), so a window of 1 is the
! amount itself and a window past the rows is the running total. An amount
! below 0 (energy, water and land are never negative) or a width outside
! 1..999999 makes ok 0 and every total a division by zero: refused. A sum
! past 64 bits is refused by Trebago itself, never wrapped. Row j is inside
! row i's window when j <= i and j > i - width, which
! min(1, max(0, i - j + 1)) * min(1, max(0, j - i + width)) is for integers.
trebago rolling
  in  amount(n), width
  out total(n)
  var s(n), ok
  ok = min(1, max(0, width)) * min(1, max(0, 999999 - width + 1)) &
     * (1 - min(1, sum(i, min(1, max(0, 0 - amount(i))))))
  s(i) = sum(j, amount(j) * min(1, max(0, i - j + 1)) * min(1, max(0, j - i + width)))
  total(i) = s(i) / ok
end
